invariant: INV-16
file: src/poly1305_vector.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: the last pass multiplies both lanes by the powers every pass
  before it takes, so the odd blocks of the last pass, and every odd
  block before them, are owed one power of r more than they get. The
  tag is wrong for every update the path takes. CBMC cannot read an
  intrinsic, so no proof covers this file, and bin/poly1305_equiv_test
  holds its accumulator to poly1305.c's after every update.

--- old
    multipliers_set(of_r, pairs, 1);
--- new
    multipliers_set(of_r, pairs, 0);
